Brihanmumbai Municipal Commissioner Smt. Ashwini Bhide shared her insights in a Fireside chat held on “Building a City Sustainably: Growth, Resilience and Liveability” as a part of the Social Impact Summit organised by The Times of India at Taj Lands End in Bandra West. 

The spirit of Mumbai makes it possible to undertake several landmark projects she said and challenging infrastructure works like the underground Mumbai Metro, Coastal Road and Eastern Freeway are examples of this spirit. “Sustainability is a long-term commitment and is considered at every stage of planning and implementation of projects in Mumbai. Environmental sustainability, biodiversity and climate related considerations are given due importance and are translated into action on the ground,” said Smt. Ashwini Bhide.

At the same time, citizen participation is crucial to effective urban governance and the success of civic projects. Smt. Ashwini Bhide therefore appealed to citizens to contribute actively towards making Mumbai more sustainable and liveable.

